  "readmeExcerpt": "<img src=\"https://github.com/opa334/Dopamine/assets/52459150/ed04dd3e-d879-456d-9aa3-d4ed44819c7e\" width=\"64\" />\n\n# Dopamine\n\nA rootless semi-untethered jailbreak for iOS 15.0 - 17.3.1 (arm64e), iOS 15.0 - 18.7.1, 26.0 - 26.0.1 (A12/A13) and iOS 15.0 - 18.7.1 (arm64). More details will follow here soon.\n\nPlease note that all issues related to version support will be deleted without response.\n\nOfficial website / download: https://ellekit.space/dopamine/\n",
  "readmeHtml": "<div id=\"readme\" class=\"md\" data-path=\"README.md\"><article class=\"markdown-body entry-content container-lg\" itemprop=\"text\"><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://private-user-images.githubusercontent.com/52459150/238158404-ed04dd3e-d879-456d-9aa3-d4ed44819c7e.png?jwt=eyJ0eXAiOiJKV1QiLCJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9..N-T0Uv9Kzw_FL9YVthxYBuRkO34ZypFUC6XYjjrkd4s\"><img src=\"https://private-user-images.githubusercontent.com/52459150/238158404-ed04dd3e-d879-456d-9aa3-d4ed44819c7e.png?jwt=eyJ0eXAiOiJKV1QiLCJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9..N-T0Uv9Kzw_FL9YVthxYBuRkO34ZypFUC6XYjjrkd4s\" width=\"64\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"></a>\n<div class=\"markdown-heading\" dir=\"auto\"><h1 class=\"heading-element\" dir=\"auto\">Dopamine</h1></div>\n<p dir=\"auto\">A rootless semi-untethered jailbreak for iOS 15.0 - 17.3.1 (arm64e), iOS 15.0 - 18.7.1, 26.0 - 26.0.1 (A12/A13) and iOS 15.0 - 18.7.1 (arm64). More details will follow here soon.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Please note that all issues related to version support will be deleted without response.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Official website / download: <a href=\"https://ellekit.space/dopamine/\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://ellekit.space/dopamine/</a></p>\n</article></div>",
  "releases": [
    {
      "name": "3.0.4",
      "tag": "3.0.4",
      "url": "https://github.com/opa334/Dopamine/releases/tag/3.0.4",
      "publishedAt": "2026-08-09T13:08:08Z",
      "prerelease": false,
      "body": "- Fix missing post exploitation clean up if the jailbreak failed or is being removed",
      "downloads": 28145,
      "reactions": 67
    },
    {
      "name": "3.0.2",
      "tag": "3.0.2",
      "url": "https://github.com/opa334/Dopamine/releases/tag/3.0.2",
      "publishedAt": "2026-08-09T02:37:16Z",
      "prerelease": false,
      "body": "- Fix random panics on TXM devices when something tries to load a dynamic trustcache\r\n- Fix non CS_ADHOC libraries not being loadable on TXM devices in certain processes for which fcntl(F_ADDSIGS, ...) is blocked by sandbox (Fixes some tweaks not working)\r\n- Fix binaries and libraries signed with a team id not working on TXM devices\r\n- Fix crashes with some apps that were installed by TrollStore Lite on iOS 17.0 - 17.3.1\r\n- Fix momentarius not working on older iOS versions (by @staturnzz)\r\n- Minor improvements to DarkSword and ClearSword (by @TheRealClarity)\r\n- Fix support for iOS 18.1 beta 4 (A12/A13)",
      "downloads": 8579,
      "reactions": 43
    },
    {
      "name": "3.0.1",
      "tag": "3.0.1",
      "url": "https://github.com/opa334/Dopamine/releases/tag/3.0.1",
      "publishedAt": "2026-08-07T23:20:15Z",
      "prerelease": false,
      "body": "- Fix Titan not working on ARM_LARGE_MEMORY kernels (Mainly M1/M2 iPads)\r\n- Fix XPF being broken on some iOS 15.x versions\r\n- Fix kfd exploits being broken on iOS 16.x\r\n- Fix ClearSword / DarkSword showing up as supported even on devices that do not support them\r\n- In DarkSword / ClearSword workaround message, add notice about A8 possibly requiring multiple attempts\r\n- Enable support for iOS 26.1 beta 1 - 3 (A12/A13)\r\n\r\n(All of the issues fixed were regressions from 3.0)",
      "downloads": 25144,
      "reactions": 121
    },
    {
      "name": "3.0",
      "tag": "3.0",
      "url": "https://github.com/opa334/Dopamine/releases/tag/3.0",
      "publishedAt": "2026-08-07T18:51:04Z",
      "prerelease": false,
      "body": "- Add Titan PPL/SPTM bypass by @alfiecg24, introduces support for all devices running 16.5.1 - 17.3.1\r\n- Add momentarius PPL bypass by @staturnzz and @TheRealClarity, introduces support for A12/A13 devices running 16.6 - 18.7.1, 26.0 - 26.0.1\r\n- Add support for SPTM devices up to 27.0 betas in general, can be tested on Corellium devices using the install script at Standalone/Corellium, obviously only works up to 17.3.1 on real devices due to lack of an SPTM bypass on >=17.4\r\n- Add ClearSword exploit by @TheRealClarity, cleaner alternative to DarkSword that seems to have better reliability\r\n- Add workaround for DarkSword/ClearSword not working on A8 iPads, iPad 5, iPad 6 and iPad Pro 9.7\" contributed by @sk8ingDuck, involves a respring through a respring method contributed by @wh1te4ever\r\n- Fix various issues with the Dopamine app from the 2.5 Betas, such as settings not saving\r\n- Fix various issues with installing apps via TrollStore Lite on iOS 17.4+\r\n- More secure method of detecting the Dopamine app that jailbroke the device by saving it's id when intially jailbreaking and later comparing against it, should also solve issues when a signing tool renames the .app bundle\r\n\r\nNOTES:\r",
      "downloads": 9798,
      "reactions": 149
    },
    {
      "name": "2.5 Beta 4",
      "tag": "2.5b4",
      "url": "https://github.com/opa334/Dopamine/releases/tag/2.5b4",
      "publishedAt": "2026-06-05T14:58:45Z",
      "prerelease": true,
      "body": "- Fix support for iOS 17.1 - 17.3.1\r\n\r\nKnown issues\r\n- DarkSword currently does not support 2GB RAM devices running iOS 17.0 or higher (e.g. iPad 6)\r\n- Zebra crashes on launch on some newer iOS versions due to a missing entitlement, this will be fixed soon\r\n- DarkSword currently does not support A8(X)\r\n- DarkSword currently may not work on A9X\r\n- DarkSword currently may not work on early iOS 16 versions (presumably 16.0 - 16.3.1)\r\n- DarkSword may sometimes fail and make the Dopamine app close\r\n- The version in Dopamine will show as 2.4.99, this is to prevent issues with the in-app updater",
      "downloads": 54460,
      "reactions": 114
    }
  ],
